OL,3,GNEWSATeam with a head for heights keeps
OL,4,Acathedral safe from lightning
OL,5,
OL,6,F"It's a weird job, to say you're going
OL,7,Fto be up that high on a Monday morning
OL,8,Fwhen most people might be sat in an
OL,9,Foffice," says Neil Fillery, peering out
OL,10,Ffrom the highest point of Lincoln
OL,11,FCathedral.
OL,13,FSurrounded by the cries of the resident
OL,14,Fperegrine falcons, lightning protection
OL,15,Fengineer Fillery and steeplejack
OL,16,FMateusz Pierwola climb a ladder to the
OL,17,Ftop of the central tower's four
OL,18,Fpinnacles.
OL,20,F"It's such a thrill when you get up
OL,21,Fthere," he says.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,387,380,200,160,0,100
